{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/na18b2tc","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":48,"top":145,"width":864,"height":360},"name":"Submission content","text":"THE CHALLENGE\nA single unanswered or declined offer can stall a donation even when other recipients could collect it in time. Manual follow-up also makes it difficult to track partial quantities and pickup completion.\n\nOUR APPROACH\n• Filter for recipient eligibility, capacity, food preferences, and pickup timing.\n• Rank feasible offers using a transparent score: deadline 35%, capacity 30%, distance 20%, preferences 15%. Distance is a synthetic demo estimate, not live routing.\n• Revalidate and reserve portions on acceptance; a decline does not consume stock.\n• Expire timed-out offers and rematch remaining portions before the pickup deadline.\n\nUSP: explainable recovery with auditable state changes and pickup tracking kept separate from allocation.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18,"typeface":"Google Sans Flex","color":"#202124","alignment":"left"}}
